    "blocks": [
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Spring MVC allows for mapping the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "DispatcherServlet"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " to "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "/"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " (thus overriding the mapping of the container’s default Servlet), while still allowing static resource requests to be handled by the container’s default Servlet. It configures a "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "DefaultServletHttpRequestHandler"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " with a URL mapping of "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "/**"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " and the lowest priority relative to other URL mappings."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "This handler forwards all requests to the default Servlet. Therefore, it must remain last in the order of all other URL "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "HandlerMappings"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ". That is the case if you use "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "<mvc:annotation-driven>"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ". Alternatively, if you set up your own customized "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "HandlerMapping"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " instance, be sure to set its "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "order"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " property to a value lower than that of the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "DefaultServletHttpRequestHandler"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ", which is "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Integer.MAX_VALUE"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "The following example shows how to enable the feature by using the default setup:"
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "include-code::./WebConfiguration[tag=snippet,indent=0]"
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "The caveat to overriding the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "/"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " Servlet mapping is that the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "RequestDispatcher"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " for the default Servlet must be retrieved by name rather than by path. The "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "DefaultServletHttpRequestHandler"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " tries to auto-detect the default Servlet for the container at startup time, using a list of known names for most of the major Servlet containers (including Tomcat, Jetty, GlassFish, JBoss, WebLogic, and WebSphere). If the default Servlet has been custom-configured with a different name, or if a different Servlet container is being used where the default Servlet name is unknown, then you must explicitly provide the default Servlet’s name, as the following example shows:"
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "include-code::./CustomDefaultServletConfiguration[tag=snippet,indent=0]"
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      }
    ],
    "outline": null,
    "title": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "value": "Default Servlet"
      }
    ]
  }
}
